    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15727" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕnarmŏnius</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕnhar-</span></b> , also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-monĭ-cus</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναρμόνιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>enharmonic;</i> as <i>subst.</i> (sc.
			melodiae genus), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναρμόνιον
			μέλος</span>, <i>the technical name in Greek music
				of a kind of melody</i>, in which quarter-tones predominated,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 930</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modulatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9, § 942 al.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2, 4,
		13</span></i>.</div>
